                        "sense_id": "94056995-51a7-3c38-b915-693f92b457ea",
                        "entry_id": "eedd4300-1efc-389f-8c2b-be2e1b477c49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A creature with many feet, especially a centipede, millepede or similar creature."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c005e90e-d382-46ab-8cf6-5d28a9851b16",
                                "sense_id": "94056995-51a7-3c38-b915-693f92b457ea",
                                "text": "XLVI. THE Ambua, ſo the Natives of Brazil call the Millepedes and the Centipedes Serpents. […]\nIN theſe Multipedes, the Mechaniſm of the Body is very curious; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3bb83c7-b477-46ea-bbdf-cc3c325e8fb6",
                                "sense_id": "94056995-51a7-3c38-b915-693f92b457ea",
                                "text": "In the course of two weeks there developed in all the aquaria minute crustaceans (shell insects, flea lobsters, water multipedes, infusoria, green algae), a felted mass […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00f72a3e-c68e-433b-b757-c0f0ab4e88be",
                                "sense_id": "94056995-51a7-3c38-b915-693f92b457ea",
                                "text": "Animals exhibit differences in the number of their feet, and accordingly have been distributed into classes, consisting of bipeds, quadrupeds, and multipedes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3edadf75-9076-3497-8b9c-c8fb61ba682d",
                        "entry_id": "eedd4300-1efc-389f-8c2b-be2e1b477c49",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A branching structure with many separate termini."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56197bf8-f62c-4b16-9c9d-84577eab649e",
                                "sense_id": "3edadf75-9076-3497-8b9c-c8fb61ba682d",
                                "text": "The stability of the mesophases for the polypedes and multipedes is reported in Table 17."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8d1ec94-3e78-4d50-a0a8-dfab36dc6d36",
                                "sense_id": "3edadf75-9076-3497-8b9c-c8fb61ba682d",
                                "text": "As noted in Section 15.1, the design of multipedes allows the incorporation of functional moieties into self-assembling and/or self-organizing states of matter."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
